    "explanation": "Both parties agree this was an on-demand booking at Joo Koon Bus Interchange with no scheduled pickup time. The record shows the driver arrived at 07:42:00 and that his arrival is corroborated by his GPS trace: the nearest fix in the arrival window, at 07:43:00, was 127.46 m from the pin with a reported 6 m accuracy, inside the 150 m arrival radius POL-NS-21 sets for a transport hub (TRANSPORT_HUB). Because the trip is on-demand, the 300-second free wait ran from arrival; it expired at 07:47:00 and the driver cancelled at 07:48:30, 390 seconds after arrival and 90 seconds after the free wait ended. Before cancelling he had sent two in-app messages (07:42:20 and 07:45:30, both read) and placed one in-app call (07:44:10, unanswered, ringing 30 s), so POL-NS-23's contact obligation was satisfied and the fee is not voided. POL-NS-24 is not engaged: the trip had no scheduled time and the driver did arrive, and in any event the rider did not cancel. The fare ledger records exactly one cancellation fee of 5.00 SGD, matching POL-NS-22's 5.00 SGD, so the fee stands. On the rider's points: the argument that the driver was 127 m from the pin does not help you, rider — 127 m is inside the policy's own 150 m arrival tolerance for this pickup, and the driver's own messages placing him 'beside the interchange exit' and 'near the taxi stand' are consistent with that. Your account that you were at the pin and he was not is a genuine disagreement, but no clause this dispute turns on — POL-NS-21, POL-NS-22, POL-NS-23 — makes the rider's location a fact the ruling needs; the empty rider track therefore does not open POL-GEN-26, and the 5.00 SGD is not held back on that basis. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-06060-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and no clause requires it; likewise no repeat-no-show referral arises because the rider's no_show_cancellations_30d counter does not appear in the profile. Driven by the filing frame: you filed, driver, and the whole 5.00 SGD no-show fee stands, so the 5.00 SGD already refunded to the rider and recovered from you is returned to you. Both amount fields carry the same 5.00 SGD figure the ruling moves; no referral issues (POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not fire because contact was attempted, POL-NS-25 does not fire, and the fee is the standard 5.00 SGD so POL-NS-22's fee-amount check does not fire)."
